@8307. Under <Mercy>, see this reference.

@8321. That thus, without danger of infestation, all will be saved who are in the faculty of receiving the truth of good and the good of truth. Signified, Explained.

@--. For, so long as the evil had not been cast into Hell, scarcely any could "pass over," that is, be saved. Explained.

@--[end]. As it is charity which gives (the above-named) faculty, it is charity which saves; for those who are saved, are not saved through charity from themselves, but through charity from the Lord, consequently through this faculty of receiving.

@8387. He who wants to be saved, must confess his sins, and perform repentance. Explained.

@8408[4]. The Salvation of the faithful. Ti.

@8543. (The inhabitants of Jupiter) do not worship the Lord as a King; but as a Saviour.

