@--[4]. (There) all are consociated according to their life... hence it is not possible for the evil and the good to be together; nor is it possible for those to be in good who are evil; for good and evil are opposites, and the one destroys the other: (thus) it is not possible that those in Hell should be saved; thus it is not feasible that Salvation, however a man had lived, should be from mercy alone.

